{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Discovered from sole-curbable-stinkpot (9a71-ba9b-89d0-4cb8). The original framing understated\nthis: the string is not swallowed noise, it is a FAILURE COUNTED AS A SUCCESS. Re-scoped.\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nIn the outbound link-apply loop, a cancelled ACLI link delete is counted as an applied link,\nso `RECON: batch_outcome ... error=None links_applied=N` reports work that never happened and\nthe silent-noop canary is blind to it by construction.\n\nEvidence, run 31535962079 raw log:\n\n- `ACLI stderr: X Error: command cancelled` occurrences = 15\n- sum of every `links_applied=` across the whole pass    = 15\n- occurrences of `update_one: ... failed`                = 0\n\nExact 1:1, per-ticket not just in aggregate (e.g. 2 cancellations -> REB-1305\n`links_applied=2`; 1 -> REB-1308 `=1`). Every ticket with zero cancellations reports\n`links_applied=0`. Zero links were actually removed in that pass.\n\nMechanism, `_update_one_dispatch_links`:\n\n    try:\n        _call_with_retry(client.delete_issue_link, link_id)\n        _links_applied += 1\n    except subprocess.CalledProcessError:\n        # ...treated as idempotent 404/409...\n        _links_applied += 1\n\nThat arm has NO print — which is why zero `update_one: ... failed` lines appear and why this\nlooked like free-floating noise. Its rationale (\"self-healing — the differ recomputes the\nREMOVE next pass\") does not hold: the cause is DETERMINISTIC. `link create`/`link delete`\nprompt for confirmation and run with `stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL`, so the prompt reads EOF and\nACLI reports `command cancelled` on every pass, forever.\n\nThis is the bug 44de silent-divergence class. `REBAR_RECONCILER_FAIL_SILENT_NOOP` cannot catch\nit: the canary tests `computed > 0 and applied == 0`, and this arm inflates `applied` to equal\n`computed`.\n\nRoot cause CONFIRMED, not suspected (see ticket comment): `acli 1.3.19-stable` — the exact\nversion the fleet caches — documents `--yes` on BOTH subcommands, and neither call site passes\nit. Verified against the link subcommands themselves, not inferred from the `workitem delete`\nsibling. `--json` IS rejected there (story 25ae, correct); `--yes` is accepted. Conflating the\ntwo flags produced the original \"verify before adding\" caution.\n\n## Approach\n\nTwo edits: stop the lie, then remove its cause.\n\n**1. Stop counting failures as applied** (`dispatch_one.py`). Add a `_links_failed` counter.\nThe delete handler's `except subprocess.CalledProcessError` arm keeps its idempotent rationale\nbut narrows to genuine idempotent signatures — stderr matching `404`, `409`, `does not exist`,\nor `not found` (case-insensitive; absent stderr is NOT idempotent). Those still count toward\n`_links_applied`, so a benign concurrent removal does not become a new hard failure. Every\nother `CalledProcessError` increments `_links_failed` and prints, as does the trailing\n`except Exception` arm and the `set_relationship` handler. Every arm stays non-fatal.\n`links_failed` rides the existing `subop` dict through `apply_handlers.py` onto the outcome\nand is printed in the `batch_outcome` line — an additive field. This alone lets the canary\nfire.\n\n**2. Remove the cause** (`acli_graph.py`). Pass `--yes` to `workitem link create` and\n`workitem link delete`, with a comment citing the 1.3.19-stable help verification, mirroring\nthe existing `workitem delete` precedent at `acli.py:714-724` (bug 3256 / live cfd6 probe).\n\n**Deliberately NOT doing:** no cancellation fast-abort / typed error. With `--yes` removing\nthe prompt, that is speculative machinery for a path that should stop occurring; edit 1 makes\nany residual failure visible, which is the durable protection.\n\n**Disjointness.** This is the OUTBOUND ACLI path: it shares no edit region with change 1640's\n`_AUTH_FAILURE_MARKERS` / `AcliAuthError` (credential rejection, different markers and call\npath) or with the inbound-links state work.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_one.py` — `_links_failed`; narrowed idempotent\n  arm; create-side failure counting. `_update_one_dispatch_links` becomes\n  `(computed, applied, failed)`; that arity change is contained to one production caller plus\n  two call sites in `test_capability_guard_a3fa.py`, all updated. Two size gates bite and are\n  handled rather than blessed: the REMOVE sub-phase is extracted into `_dispatch_link_removes`\n  along the ADD/REMOVE seam (the narrowed arm puts the parent one over its LOCKED complexity\n  ceiling of 17), and the link phase then moves to the sibling leaf below, since\n  `dispatch_one.py` crosses the 800-LOC cap.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_apply_phases.py` — receives the link-dispatch\n  cluster. The existing seam, not an arbitrary slice: the phase already calls four helpers\n  living there (`_call_with_retry`, `_capability_present`, `_find_link_id`,\n  `_index_existing_links`), so the move REMOVES cross-module reach and lands beside its\n  sibling `_update_one_dispatch_comments`. `dispatch_one` re-imports it, so\n  `dispatch_one.<name>` access is unchanged.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_handlers.py` — carry `links_failed` onto outcome.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/applier.py` — print `links_failed` in `batch_outcome`.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_graph.py` — `--yes` on both link cmds.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_outbound_link_failure_accounting.py` (new).\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_capability_guard_a3fa.py` — unpacks\n  `_update_one_dispatch_links` at two call sites; updated to the 3-tuple, and its real-failure\n  case now also asserts `failed == 1`, which is what separates it from the designed\n  capability skip it sits beside.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_link_removal_sync.py` — its\n  `test_update_one_tolerates_acli_delete_failure` asserts `links_applied == 1` for a\n  `CalledProcessError` with **no stderr**; that ENCODES the defect and flips to\n  `links_applied == 0, links_failed == 1`. Its real intent (\"does not raise, pass not\n  unwound\") is preserved, and a `404`-stderr sibling keeps idempotent-race coverage.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: a create + delete that both succeed report `links_applied=2 links_failed=0`.\n- Regression (the defect): a `delete_issue_link` raising `CalledProcessError` with\n  `command cancelled` stderr yields `links_applied=0 links_failed=1`, not `links_applied=1`.\n- Idempotent path preserved: the same failure with `404` stderr still counts applied.\n- Absent stderr is not idempotent: `CalledProcessError` with `stderr=None` counts failed.\n- Edge: `set_relationship` failure increments `links_failed`, returns normally (non-fatal).\n- Argv: `link create` and `link delete` argv both contain `--yes`, and still no `--json`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A cancelled `delete_issue_link` (non-idempotent stderr) no longer increments\n      `links_applied` — verified by a test asserting `links_applied=0, links_failed=1`.\n- [ ] A failed `delete_issue_link` with idempotent stderr (404/409/does-not-exist/not-found)\n      still counts applied — verified by a test asserting `links_applied=1, links_failed=0`.\n- [ ] `CalledProcessError` with `stderr=None` counts failed, not applied — verified by test.\n- [ ] A failed `set_relationship` increments `links_failed` and does not unwind the pass —\n      verified by a test asserting `links_applied=0, links_failed=1` and normal return.\n- [ ] The `RECON: batch_outcome` line for an `update` includes `links_failed=<n>` — verified\n      by a test capturing stderr and asserting the substring.\n- [ ] `workitem link create` and `workitem link delete` argv both include `--yes` — verified\n      by a test asserting the flag is present in each command list.\n- [ ] `test_update_one_tolerates_acli_delete_failure` still asserts `update_one` does not\n      raise, with its count assertion corrected to `links_applied == 0, links_failed == 1` —\n      verified by that test passing unchanged in intent.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the reconciler unit suite pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786533236518056001,"uuid":"ad5acb0a-12a1-499f-bb30-21018f592b5b"}